WEBVTT

00:00:13.578 --> 00:00:16.755
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log,
stardate 58130.6.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:16.798 --> 00:00:19.758
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;has rendezvoused
with theArchimedes&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.761
&lt;i&gt;and my old friend
Captain Sonya Gomez&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:22.804 --> 00:00:26.112
&lt;i&gt;so that we can assist in her
first contact of the Lapeerians.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:26.156 --> 00:00:27.896
The Laap System is

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.985
a gas giant,
couple Class Js,

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.422
obviously our new Class M,

00:00:31.465 --> 00:00:33.728
and an unstable planetoid
right here,

00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:35.556
just off its ecliptic.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.689
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; will be positioned
outside the system.

00:00:37.732 --> 00:00:40.561
Isn't that overly cautious
for a planetoid?

00:00:40.605 --> 00:00:42.824
Carol, I know &lt;i&gt;
Cali&lt;/i&gt;-class isn't afraid

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.565
of getting their nacelles dirty.

00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:46.698
We just don't want multiple
ships approaching at once,

00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:48.917
or the Lapeerians
might mistake "first contact"

00:00:48.961 --> 00:00:51.006
- for a "first invasion."
- Of course.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.660
Once formalities are complete,

00:00:52.704 --> 00:00:54.619
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; can install
subspace transponders

00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:56.664
and join us for a celebration
with the locals.

00:00:56.708 --> 00:00:59.711
I'll tell sickbay
to brace for hangovers.

00:00:59.754 --> 00:01:01.321
One more thing,
Captain Freeman.

00:01:01.365 --> 00:01:05.282
I've heard that
congratulations are in order.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.201
Oh, great. Jennifer.

00:01:11.244 --> 00:01:13.290
I'm sure you just love
catching me with contraband,

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:15.553
but can you try not to rat me
out to Ransom this time, okay?

00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:16.684
Yeah, I don't care.

00:01:16.728 --> 00:01:18.121
Oh, please, I know you hate me.

00:01:18.164 --> 00:01:20.297
Pfft, I don't think
about you at all.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.820
Yeah, right,
I bet you dream about me

00:01:21.863 --> 00:01:23.996
every night with your
stupid little butt--

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:25.345
Whoa.

00:01:25.389 --> 00:01:26.868
Enjoy your final mission
on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:29.001
New ships are exciting,

00:01:29.044 --> 00:01:30.176
you'll miss your crew.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.699
You don't think the admiralty

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:33.527
will let me transfer
my senior staff?

00:01:33.571 --> 00:01:35.181
With &lt;i&gt;California&lt;/i&gt;-class?

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:37.879
Command likes to keep
a real sense of consistency.

00:01:37.923 --> 00:01:41.013
You're gonna have to make
some tearful goodbyes.

00:02:57.394 --> 00:02:59.700
Aw, man, this again?

00:02:59.744 --> 00:03:01.789
Hey, Boimler, my implant's
messing up my vision.

00:03:01.833 --> 00:03:03.617
Can you take my shift
in Cetacean Ops

00:03:03.661 --> 00:03:05.750
- so I can get it fixed?
- Sorry, I can't.

00:03:05.793 --> 00:03:07.273
Captain Freeman Day's
only a week away.

00:03:07.317 --> 00:03:09.057
My decorations have
to be the best.

00:03:09.101 --> 00:03:10.972
Isn't that a craft day
for toddlers?

00:03:11.016 --> 00:03:13.061
- Not anymore.

00:03:13.105 --> 00:03:15.325
Hey. I-I was just hiding
behind a bush

00:03:15.368 --> 00:03:17.022
and I heard the captain's
getting a promotion.

00:03:17.065 --> 00:03:18.589
Whoa, really? Good for her.

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:21.026
Bad for us! I don't want
a whole new captain.

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:23.376
We could end up with some weirdo
with a riding crop.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.117
Yeah, but this is huge
for your mom.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.641
She gets to dive into
the unknown on a whole new ship.

00:03:27.685 --> 00:03:29.600
Gah, I never get to dive
into unknowns.

00:03:29.643 --> 00:03:32.472
Ooh, a promotion means
a big party and a fancy dinner.

00:03:32.516 --> 00:03:34.387
- I hope it's fajitas.
- Ooh. Ooh, ooh,

00:03:34.431 --> 00:03:36.041
then we get to line up
in the hallway, right?

00:03:36.084 --> 00:03:37.825
And then we all applaud

00:03:37.869 --> 00:03:40.219
while the captain walks off
the ship for the last time.

00:03:40.263 --> 00:03:41.612
Ooh, that sounds great!

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:43.309
It sounds like betrayal,
but with clapping.

00:03:43.353 --> 00:03:44.789
Ugh, this is totally
going to ruin

00:03:44.832 --> 00:03:46.312
the timing for
Captain Freeman Day.

00:03:46.356 --> 00:03:47.879
You think Ransom might be
willing to move it up?

00:03:47.922 --> 00:03:49.315
It is a vanity holiday

00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:50.795
to trick kids
into respecting authority,

00:03:50.838 --> 00:03:52.275
plus she hasn't even
told Ransom...

00:03:52.318 --> 00:03:53.885
And he'd probably
be super pissed.

00:03:53.928 --> 00:03:55.756
Thanks, Boimler!
- Mariner, no.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.715
Mariner! Ah!
That wasn't my idea!

00:04:00.413 --> 00:04:01.980
Oh, no.

00:04:02.023 --> 00:04:03.851
Dr. T'Ana wants to see me
in her office.

00:04:03.895 --> 00:04:05.157
I think she's mad at me.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.289
For what?

00:04:06.332 --> 00:04:07.855
Ugh, well, I mean,

00:04:07.899 --> 00:04:09.466
there's just so much
to study on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:09.509 --> 00:04:10.945
sometimes it's hard to stay
focused on just sickbay.

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:13.252
Come on. Dr. T's grouchy,
and you're great.

00:04:13.296 --> 00:04:14.601
I'm sure you're overthinking it.

00:04:14.645 --> 00:04:15.733
Aw, thank you, Rutherford.

00:04:15.776 --> 00:04:16.864
You're welcome.

00:04:16.908 --> 00:04:18.692
Well, I guess I'll head off.

00:04:18.736 --> 00:04:20.912
You don't think this alert will
mess with my work, do you?

00:04:20.955 --> 00:04:22.479
Hello?

00:04:22.522 --> 00:04:24.307
Tendi?

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.222
She says "hi" to everyone,
she's a waitress.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.050
But it's different.
She's, like, so attentive.

00:04:29.094 --> 00:04:30.530
I mean, always asking
what I'm doing...

00:04:30.574 --> 00:04:32.619
Yo, what's up?
Talking about bridge crew stuff?

00:04:32.663 --> 00:04:33.925
Tough gig, tough gig.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.535
Uh, this booth's full, Ensign.

00:04:35.579 --> 00:04:37.232
I get it, yeah, no,

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.060
and you want to maintain
the illusion of command, yeah.

00:04:39.104 --> 00:04:41.193
It's not an illusion.
I'm your commander.

00:04:41.236 --> 00:04:42.716
Sure. I'll take off, but first,

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.109
I think I have something

00:04:44.152 --> 00:04:46.241
that you guys are going
to want to hear.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.287
Yeah, so I was on the station...

00:05:03.824 --> 00:05:07.088
&lt;i&gt;We'll see you in the
Laap system, Captain Freeman.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:07.132 --> 00:05:08.916
Looking forward to it,
Captain Gomez.

00:05:13.094 --> 00:05:14.487
Ransom, take us out.

00:05:14.531 --> 00:05:16.228
Oh, is it time to go?

00:05:16.271 --> 00:05:19.884
Thank you so much for
all that information, Captain.

00:05:19.927 --> 00:05:21.712
Okay...

00:05:21.755 --> 00:05:24.149
Shaxs, any update
on those phaser repairs?

00:05:24.192 --> 00:05:26.978
No. And if there was an update,
I would tell you.

00:05:27.021 --> 00:05:30.024
I wouldn't keep that information
to myself. I'm an open book!

00:05:30.068 --> 00:05:32.549
Did someone buy
an alien mood-altering plant

00:05:32.592 --> 00:05:34.202
on the station or something?

00:05:34.246 --> 00:05:35.508
Maybe everyone feels like
they should know more

00:05:35.552 --> 00:05:37.336
about what's going on
on the ship.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.164
Like need-to-know stuff
that they don't know, you know?

00:05:39.207 --> 00:05:41.209
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is ready
for warp, Captain.

00:05:41.253 --> 00:05:42.559
You know, your ship?

00:05:42.602 --> 00:05:44.256
Oh. Just warp me already.

00:05:44.299 --> 00:05:47.346
Senior staff,
in my ready room. Now.

00:05:52.046 --> 00:05:54.266
Look, at this point,
it's pretty clear

00:05:54.309 --> 00:05:56.399
she's not cut out for Medical.

00:05:57.661 --> 00:05:59.402
What? No!

00:06:00.925 --> 00:06:01.969
What the hell is going on here?

00:06:02.013 --> 00:06:03.318
I heard you and Gomez,

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.016
- back on the station.
- Heard what?

00:06:05.059 --> 00:06:06.887
That you're being offered
a promotion to a new ship,

00:06:06.931 --> 00:06:09.150
and while I can assume
I'll remain at your side,

00:06:09.194 --> 00:06:10.761
everyone else here
is pretty upset.

00:06:10.804 --> 00:06:12.066
Who said I'm taking you with me?

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.590
- You aren't?
- So you are leaving?

00:06:13.633 --> 00:06:15.374
Why didn't you tell us?

00:06:15.418 --> 00:06:17.898
You're lucky I'm so spiritually
centered or I'd snap!

00:06:17.942 --> 00:06:19.422
It's not official.

00:06:19.465 --> 00:06:21.554
Why the hell wouldn't you take
your number one?

00:06:21.598 --> 00:06:23.208
I agree with you
at all times!

00:06:23.251 --> 00:06:25.340
I would transfer all of you
if I could,

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.907
but Command doesn't like

00:06:26.951 --> 00:06:28.431
shuffling crews
off &lt;i&gt;California&lt;/i&gt;-cla...

00:06:28.474 --> 00:06:30.650
Oh, that's such
[bleep]!

00:06:30.694 --> 00:06:32.522
We are just as good as
any other class!

00:06:32.565 --> 00:06:34.175
Our warp core is
twice as fast

00:06:34.219 --> 00:06:36.439
as any other ship
in the fleet!

00:06:36.482 --> 00:06:38.136
Whoa! Mr. Billups...

00:06:38.179 --> 00:06:40.138
Oh, hey. So who's going
to be the new captain?

00:06:40.181 --> 00:06:41.966
Come on, who else would it be?

00:06:42.009 --> 00:06:44.838
- They'll be bringing
on someone new.
- What?!

00:06:44.882 --> 00:06:46.536
This is ridiculous!
Are you saying...

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:50.061
- Rutherford!
- Hey!

00:06:50.104 --> 00:06:51.192
How'd it go with Dr. T?

00:06:51.236 --> 00:06:52.542
I-I didn't talk to her.

00:06:52.585 --> 00:06:53.847
I think she's going
to transfer me.

00:06:53.891 --> 00:06:56.371
- From Medical?
- No! Off the ship!

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:58.286
I saw her delete me
from the system.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.897
What? No way! That's crazy!

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.594
You're, like,
the nicest person in sickbay.

00:07:01.638 --> 00:07:03.683
I don't think that Dr. T'Ana
cares about being nice.

00:07:03.727 --> 00:07:04.989
She's more into hostility.

00:07:05.032 --> 00:07:06.686
Oh! I should've been more mean!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.296
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
I gotta see this for myself.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.297
Hang on.

00:07:09.341 --> 00:07:10.777
You're right.

00:07:10.821 --> 00:07:12.605
You're not in there!
That's so unfair.

00:07:12.649 --> 00:07:13.867
I can't believe this.

00:07:13.911 --> 00:07:16.653
I'll miss the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; so much.

00:07:18.568 --> 00:07:21.266
Then let's make sure you see
her one last time. Come on.

00:07:21.309 --> 00:07:23.007
- W-What do you mean?
- Let's go visit

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.399
all your favorite places
on the ship,

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:25.836
so you can have
a proper goodbye.

00:07:25.879 --> 00:07:28.055
- That's a great idea.
- Ow!

00:07:28.099 --> 00:07:30.275
- Uh, maybe I should
lead the way.

00:07:30.318 --> 00:07:32.582
Yeah,
that's an okey dokey from me.

00:07:40.938 --> 00:07:42.766
All scans nominal,
Captain Gomez.

00:07:42.809 --> 00:07:44.071
Welcome to the Laap system.

00:07:44.115 --> 00:07:45.551
Take us in nice and slow.

00:07:45.595 --> 00:07:47.597
Let's give them plenty of time
to scan us.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.120
Nobody likes unexpected guests.

00:07:49.163 --> 00:07:50.382
Ah!

00:07:50.425 --> 00:07:51.905
Uh, I'm okay.

00:07:51.949 --> 00:07:53.211
Please don't, it's fine.

00:07:53.254 --> 00:07:54.255
Don't worry about it.

00:07:54.299 --> 00:07:55.779
I've done way worse

00:07:55.822 --> 00:07:58.172
in front of much more
intimidating captains.

00:08:02.437 --> 00:08:04.527
Ah. Maintenance hatch 788,

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.485
always warm to the touch.

00:08:06.529 --> 00:08:07.573
- Ow!

00:08:08.922 --> 00:08:11.055
Little ship,
but a big warp core.

00:08:11.098 --> 00:08:13.536
Oh, listen to that thrum.

00:08:14.885 --> 00:08:16.626
- Ah!
- Whoa.

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:22.196
This is where we watched
the Trivoli pulsar.

00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:24.938
They-they always tell you

00:08:24.982 --> 00:08:26.723
not to get too attached
to your ship.

00:08:26.766 --> 00:08:28.899
But how could you not?

00:08:28.942 --> 00:08:31.249
Hey, can I tell you something?

00:08:31.292 --> 00:08:32.424
Y-Yeah?

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:33.991
I am attached to the ship.

00:08:34.034 --> 00:08:35.427
I love the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:36.950
I have for a long time now.

00:08:36.994 --> 00:08:38.473
And no one can tell me
otherwise!

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:41.215
I love the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt; too.

00:08:42.347 --> 00:08:44.044
Ooh, I know where
we should go next.

00:08:44.088 --> 00:08:45.437
Somewhere off-limits.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.786
The rubber ducky room?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:47.961
Better.

00:08:48.614 --> 00:08:50.137
&lt;i&gt;Not fair! Not fair!&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:50.181 --> 00:08:51.138
- That job is mine!

00:08:51.182 --> 00:08:52.183
That job is mine!

00:08:52.226 --> 00:08:53.488
Enough!

00:08:53.532 --> 00:08:54.881
Look.
Your complaints are noted.

00:08:54.925 --> 00:08:56.187
Now get back
to your stations.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.536
- Oh, come on!

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.842
Except you.

00:08:58.885 --> 00:09:00.278
What were you thinking?

00:09:00.321 --> 00:09:01.758
I was going to tell them
at the right time.

00:09:01.801 --> 00:09:03.411
I was trying
to avoid conflict.

00:09:03.455 --> 00:09:05.457
That's super messed up.
Those are your friends.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.633
A captain can't worry
about feelings

00:09:07.677 --> 00:09:09.679
when it comes to
a decision like this.

00:09:09.722 --> 00:09:12.246
Oh. Well, then, you're in luck,
because you don't have feelings.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.639
Gosh, you've got
so much to learn.

00:09:14.901 --> 00:09:17.077
- Report.
- The Lapeerian sun

00:09:17.121 --> 00:09:18.688
just emitted
an unpredicted flare.

00:09:18.731 --> 00:09:20.472
It's headed straight
for that planetoid!

00:10:01.339 --> 00:10:03.515
All right.
Give me the bad news.

00:10:03.558 --> 00:10:05.691
Magnetized ionic plasma
in those fragments

00:10:05.735 --> 00:10:07.301
overloaded the ship's systems.

00:10:07.345 --> 00:10:09.129
It's like we were hit
with an EMP.

00:10:09.173 --> 00:10:10.435
Warp core's off-line.

00:10:10.478 --> 00:10:11.523
What about reserves?

00:10:11.566 --> 00:10:13.133
Backup power cells are down.

00:10:13.177 --> 00:10:16.093
- Captain, it's all down.
- But... we're still moving?

00:10:16.136 --> 00:10:18.791
Momentum, plus
the Lapeerian gravity well.

00:10:18.835 --> 00:10:20.053
But that means...

00:10:20.097 --> 00:10:21.576
Unless we figure something out,

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.143
first contact is going to be

00:10:23.187 --> 00:10:24.928
us crashing into that planet.

00:10:26.494 --> 00:10:28.932
Okay, that's enough
existential dread.

00:10:28.975 --> 00:10:30.498
Let's get back to work.

00:10:32.762 --> 00:10:35.329
The &lt;i&gt;Archimedes&lt;/i&gt; took a full hit.
Her engines are down.

00:10:35.373 --> 00:10:37.723
That planetoid was stuffed
with radiolytic isotopes.

00:10:37.767 --> 00:10:38.811
They're caught
in the gravity well.

00:10:38.855 --> 00:10:40.334
20 hours until impact.

00:10:40.378 --> 00:10:43.294
Planetary damage...
it'll be catastrophic.

00:10:43.337 --> 00:10:44.730
If we can get
a tractor beam on them...

00:10:44.774 --> 00:10:46.210
Not going to happen,

00:10:46.253 --> 00:10:47.907
that debris is caught
in the orbit, too.

00:10:47.951 --> 00:10:49.735
If a piece as small as
a pomegranate hit our shields,

00:10:49.779 --> 00:10:51.389
the reaction would
knock out our systems.

00:10:52.695 --> 00:10:54.174
Hold on.
What about the deflector?

00:10:54.218 --> 00:10:56.220
I mean, isn't that
its whole job, to deflect?

00:10:56.263 --> 00:10:57.743
If we project
any sort of energy field,

00:10:57.787 --> 00:10:59.397
it'll draw the plasma
right to us.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:00.964
Can't we just warp
past the debris?

00:11:03.009 --> 00:11:04.924
That was merely a suggestion.

00:11:04.968 --> 00:11:06.317
Just break the rules.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.102
There has to be something
we can do, right?

00:11:09.146 --> 00:11:10.582
I...

00:11:10.625 --> 00:11:11.844
I don't know.

00:11:17.807 --> 00:11:19.722
The captain's yacht?
Mom, that's not going to work.

00:11:19.765 --> 00:11:21.506
It's got the same shielding
as the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:21.549 --> 00:11:23.595
Freeman.

00:11:23.638 --> 00:11:25.771
- If I can navigate
through the debris...

00:11:25.815 --> 00:11:28.382
You haven't piloted
anything in years.

00:11:28.426 --> 00:11:29.862
Please. I've still got
the hydroscoot record

00:11:29.906 --> 00:11:31.124
back at the Academy.

00:11:31.168 --> 00:11:32.473
This isn't a hydroscoot!

00:11:32.517 --> 00:11:33.692
You know what? I'll do it.

00:11:33.736 --> 00:11:35.302
No! Off my yacht!

00:11:35.346 --> 00:11:36.956
Do you think they
always come here to fight?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.479
Maybe that's why
it's off-limits.

00:11:38.523 --> 00:11:39.785
I-I don't know,

00:11:39.829 --> 00:11:41.526
but look at
all this ionic plasma.

00:11:41.569 --> 00:11:43.136
This is bad.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.616
What are you trying to prove?

00:11:44.659 --> 00:11:46.313
You already got
the promotion.

00:11:46.357 --> 00:11:47.837
Get off my yacht!
That's an order!

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.752
To let you get killed?
Uh, no way.

00:11:49.795 --> 00:11:51.101
I won't give you
the satisfaction.

00:11:51.144 --> 00:11:52.842
I'm trying to save lives.

00:11:52.885 --> 00:11:55.670
You can't just bully your way
into whatever you want.

00:11:55.714 --> 00:11:56.933
Why do you act like this?

00:11:56.976 --> 00:11:58.761
Because I'm a Kirk-style
free spirit

00:11:58.804 --> 00:12:01.024
who kicks butt and
it super intimidates people.

00:12:01.067 --> 00:12:02.547
You know that,
that's why you've always

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:04.288
protected me
from getting court-martialed.

00:12:04.331 --> 00:12:06.203
You're not a Kirk.
Kirk was confident.

00:12:06.246 --> 00:12:08.205
- So am I!
- You used to be.

00:12:08.248 --> 00:12:09.859
But now the only thing
you're confident of

00:12:09.902 --> 00:12:11.643
is that everything has
to be a fight.

00:12:11.686 --> 00:12:14.037
You have to drop your defenses
and make some allies.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.647
- That's it!
Whoa!

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.823
Rutherford!
Were you, were you spying on us?

00:12:17.867 --> 00:12:19.216
I think I know how to save
the &lt;i&gt;Archimedes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:19.259 --> 00:12:20.783
We have to drop our defenses,

00:12:20.826 --> 00:12:22.654
like how Mariner has to do
with people.

00:12:22.697 --> 00:12:23.742
Ah, you heard that, huh?

00:12:23.786 --> 00:12:25.265
Even if we lower our shields,

00:12:25.309 --> 00:12:27.224
the hull itself has
magnetic shielding.

00:12:27.267 --> 00:12:28.747
There's no way to discharge it.

00:12:28.791 --> 00:12:31.576
Yes. So we remove the hull.

00:12:31.619 --> 00:12:33.186
Whoa.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.840
Okay, uh, we do kind of
need that to, you know,

00:12:34.884 --> 00:12:36.624
like, protect us
from the vacuum of space.

00:12:36.668 --> 00:12:38.061
That's the inner hull.

00:12:38.104 --> 00:12:40.411
The outer is an extra layer
of protection...

00:12:40.454 --> 00:12:42.892
Which we wouldn't need, because
we aren't even going to warp.

00:12:42.935 --> 00:12:44.589
Wait, you guys aren't
seriously talking about

00:12:44.632 --> 00:12:46.678
- stripping the ship.
- It would take the whole crew

00:12:46.721 --> 00:12:48.854
working around the clock
to remove that many panels.

00:12:48.898 --> 00:12:51.509
Then we'd have to fly through
a dangerous debris field

00:12:51.552 --> 00:12:53.859
with zero protection,
all in 11 hours.

00:12:53.903 --> 00:12:55.034
Are you saying it can't be done?

00:12:55.078 --> 00:12:57.254
No, I'm saying we have to hurry!

00:12:58.603 --> 00:13:01.736
We'd take a serious beating,
but, Captain, this can work.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.173
Attention, all hands.

00:13:03.216 --> 00:13:04.870
Report to
your commanding officers.

00:13:04.914 --> 00:13:07.003
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Archimedes &lt;i&gt;needs our help.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:07.046 --> 00:13:08.961
&lt;i&gt;So we have to remove our hull&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:09.005 --> 00:13:10.702
&lt;i&gt;one panel at a time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:10.745 --> 00:13:13.183
&lt;i&gt;I'm calling on every officer,
no matter what&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:13.226 --> 00:13:14.662
&lt;i&gt;your usual duties are--&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:14.706 --> 00:13:16.751
&lt;i&gt;we have to work together.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:16.795 --> 00:13:18.231
&lt;i&gt;It'll be close, people;&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:18.275 --> 00:13:19.885
&lt;i&gt;our lives will be on the line.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:19.929 --> 00:13:21.539
&lt;i&gt;But we are Starfleet&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:21.582 --> 00:13:23.628
&lt;i&gt;and we never back down
from a challenge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:23.671 --> 00:13:25.238
Now, get to work.

00:13:25.282 --> 00:13:27.545
&lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; strong!

00:13:27.588 --> 00:13:29.808
&lt;i&gt;Oh, and
the ballroom dancing competition&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:29.852 --> 00:13:31.027
&lt;i&gt;will have to be postponed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:00.317 --> 00:14:02.275
Not now, not now!

00:14:02.319 --> 00:14:03.537
Problem with the coupling?

00:14:03.581 --> 00:14:04.930
No, my implant has
an error message

00:14:04.974 --> 00:14:06.236
that's covering my vision.

00:14:07.237 --> 00:14:09.152
That's odd.
Your storage is maxed out.

00:14:09.195 --> 00:14:11.197
Oh, yeah, no; that makes sense.

00:14:11.241 --> 00:14:13.591
Last year, I lost
all my memories of Tendi.

00:14:13.634 --> 00:14:15.245
So whenever I make a new one,

00:14:15.288 --> 00:14:17.595
I save three copies
just in case it happens again.

00:14:17.638 --> 00:14:18.857
Well, it's only going
to get worse

00:14:18.901 --> 00:14:19.945
until you free up some space.

00:14:19.989 --> 00:14:21.860
But what if I forget her again?

00:14:21.904 --> 00:14:24.645
Son, if you can't keep making
new memories, does it matter?

00:14:30.477 --> 00:14:34.090
Man, am I going to miss
those nacelles.

00:14:34.133 --> 00:14:36.570
We need all volatiles
deeper in the ship.

00:14:36.614 --> 00:14:37.963
Nothing explodes around here

00:14:38.007 --> 00:14:39.747
unless I'm the one
blowing it up.

00:14:39.791 --> 00:14:41.967
Sir, are you sure
this is a good idea?

00:14:42.011 --> 00:14:43.969
A powered-down viewscreen
isn't going to be any help.

00:14:44.013 --> 00:14:45.666
I need to see
where we're going.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.234
We're going to have to do this
the old-fashioned way.

00:15:05.121 --> 00:15:06.122
Try it now!

00:15:07.297 --> 00:15:08.559
Still nothing.

00:15:08.602 --> 00:15:10.256
Damn it.
With a couple of shuttles

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.562
we could redirect the ship,

00:15:11.605 --> 00:15:13.042
or at least get some crew
to safety.

00:15:13.085 --> 00:15:15.174
You should rest.
You've been up forever.

00:15:15.218 --> 00:15:17.872
I'll have a break
in seven hours either way.

00:15:17.916 --> 00:15:19.309
But in seven hours,
we'll be dea--

00:15:19.352 --> 00:15:20.701
Oh, I see what you did there.

00:15:20.745 --> 00:15:22.181
Come on.

00:15:36.152 --> 00:15:37.283
Don't phaser your foot.

00:15:37.327 --> 00:15:39.068
Just worry about your own thing.

00:15:39.111 --> 00:15:40.765
Well, at least when I'm gone

00:15:40.808 --> 00:15:42.810
you won't have anyone
pissing you off around here.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:46.292
I get it,
you're still upset.

00:15:46.336 --> 00:15:48.642
No, I'm not-- and I'm pretty &lt;i&gt;
confident&lt;/i&gt; of that.

00:15:48.686 --> 00:15:50.601
Look, all I meant was that

00:15:50.644 --> 00:15:52.037
you can still improve yourself

00:15:52.081 --> 00:15:53.560
by just opening up
to other people.

00:15:53.604 --> 00:15:55.910
You are always
trying to change me.

00:15:55.954 --> 00:15:57.695
You know what? I am glad

00:15:57.738 --> 00:15:59.218
this is your last mission here,

00:15:59.262 --> 00:16:01.090
because I never want
to work with you again.

00:16:01.133 --> 00:16:02.526
Beckett.

00:16:15.365 --> 00:16:17.541
Whoa!

00:16:17.584 --> 00:16:18.803
You okay?

00:16:20.326 --> 00:16:22.763
Dragon's blood.
Access controls are fused.

00:16:22.807 --> 00:16:24.330
We're going to have to release
this one manually.

00:16:24.374 --> 00:16:25.766
&lt;i&gt;We're out of time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.116
&lt;i&gt;Billups, tell me
we're good to go.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:27.159 --> 00:16:28.595
We still have
one more hull plate.

00:16:28.639 --> 00:16:30.597
And it's a big one.

00:16:34.645 --> 00:16:36.951
Captain, if we're going,
we have to go now.

00:16:36.995 --> 00:16:38.736
That panel's just going to have
to come off on the fly.

00:16:38.779 --> 00:16:40.042
Red alert.

00:16:40.085 --> 00:16:42.522
get us up to speed.
Carefully.

00:16:46.178 --> 00:16:48.050
Let's go, let's go!
Everyone inside, quick!

00:16:58.756 --> 00:17:00.410
Ah! Hold on.

00:17:00.453 --> 00:17:02.107
I gotta do something.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:14.119
What if someone asks
why he has it?

00:17:14.163 --> 00:17:15.338
We programmed that in.

00:17:15.381 --> 00:17:17.296
He'll think it was elective.

00:17:18.384 --> 00:17:19.777
Huh?

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.561
Ha-ha! I can see again!

00:17:21.605 --> 00:17:23.302
But I think I remembered
something I wasn't supposed to?

00:17:23.346 --> 00:17:24.738
Guys, quick!

00:17:24.782 --> 00:17:25.870
We need a hand!

00:17:25.913 --> 00:17:27.176
Cetacean Ops?

00:17:27.219 --> 00:17:28.916
But don't these guys
do navigation?

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.831
- Wait, what are we...
- Hey, Kimolu! Matt! Heads up!

00:17:37.447 --> 00:17:39.188
I would love to,
but there's no time.

00:17:39.231 --> 00:17:41.494
There's a busted hull panel
we need to release manually.

00:17:41.538 --> 00:17:43.453
Tendi and I can override
the safety protocols,

00:17:43.496 --> 00:17:44.976
but one of you guys has
to swim down

00:17:45.019 --> 00:17:46.151
and release the mag clamps.

00:17:46.195 --> 00:17:47.500
The what?
But the panel's outside.

00:17:47.544 --> 00:17:49.067
Yeah, but the control node

00:17:49.111 --> 00:17:50.590
for the manual access clamps
are down there.

00:17:50.634 --> 00:17:52.940
- Can't these two do it?

00:17:52.984 --> 00:17:55.247
Ah, yeah, it wasn't designed
for flippers.

00:17:55.291 --> 00:17:57.075
Okay, all right, sorry, sorry.

00:17:57.119 --> 00:18:00.122
Uh, once again,
Beckett Mariner saves the day.

00:18:00.165 --> 00:18:01.732
Of course my frickin' mom'll
get all the praise.

00:18:01.775 --> 00:18:03.429
Oh, shut up!

00:18:03.473 --> 00:18:05.127
You're just mad because
you don't want her to leave.

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:06.737
So what if I am, okay?

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.304
This is the most I've gotten
along with her in years,

00:18:08.347 --> 00:18:10.349
and now she decides to take off.

00:18:10.393 --> 00:18:11.437
That's messed up.

00:18:11.481 --> 00:18:12.960
And I kind of already told her

00:18:13.004 --> 00:18:15.311
I never want
to work with her again.

00:18:23.275 --> 00:18:25.756
The captain needs our support,
especially from you.

00:18:25.799 --> 00:18:27.236
Look, however this rescue goes,

00:18:27.279 --> 00:18:28.585
either we're going to be dead,

00:18:28.628 --> 00:18:30.239
or she's going to be
on a new ship.

00:18:30.282 --> 00:18:31.762
Is this really how you want
to leave things with her?

00:18:31.805 --> 00:18:33.590
Of course not!
But I can't patch things up now.

00:18:33.633 --> 00:18:35.287
I have to swim down
and unclamp a thingy...

00:18:35.331 --> 00:18:37.333
No, you don't!
Boimler's got this.

00:18:37.376 --> 00:18:38.421
You guys don't understand
my family...

00:18:38.464 --> 00:18:40.466
We are your family!

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:41.859
We will always
be there for you,

00:18:41.902 --> 00:18:43.208
And right now
we're heading into a pile

00:18:43.252 --> 00:18:45.079
of crazy dangerous space debris!

00:18:45.123 --> 00:18:46.211
Whoa. Tendi, I...

00:18:46.255 --> 00:18:47.734
Ah, no, no. Just trust us.

00:18:47.778 --> 00:18:49.736
We can do this.
Go to the bridge, apologize,

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.869
and make sure your mom
doesn't get us all killed!

00:18:51.912 --> 00:18:53.131
You guys are right.

00:18:53.175 --> 00:18:54.306
You got this, Boims?

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:55.655
Yes! Go!

00:18:55.699 --> 00:18:57.483
Thanks, okay!
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

00:18:57.527 --> 00:18:59.529
Okay, so you just gotta go
all the way down

00:18:59.572 --> 00:19:00.921
and then swim the length
of the hydrotube

00:19:00.965 --> 00:19:02.488
and then wedge
into the filter nodule

00:19:02.532 --> 00:19:03.968
to reach the clamps. Cool?

00:19:04.011 --> 00:19:06.100
Oh. Oh, wow,
that's a really long tunnel.

00:19:06.144 --> 00:19:08.233
- Uh, I'm not sure...
- Boimler, you're the one

00:19:08.277 --> 00:19:09.408
who wants to dive
into the unknown.

00:19:09.452 --> 00:19:10.540
Now's your chance.

00:19:10.583 --> 00:19:11.976
So, get diving!

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:22.508
So, you guys doing anything
for Captain Freeman Day?

00:19:49.405 --> 00:19:50.841
Approaching debris field,
Captain.

00:19:50.884 --> 00:19:53.539
Mom, I was being a jerk,
I'm sorry.

00:19:53.583 --> 00:19:55.628
I don't know why I turn
everything into a fight.

00:19:55.672 --> 00:19:57.804
I think it's because one time
after the Academy I was in...

00:19:57.848 --> 00:19:59.415
No time for emotional bids,
Ensign.

00:19:59.458 --> 00:20:01.504
Also, I was being a jerk too,

00:20:01.547 --> 00:20:02.679
- and I love you.
- Aw!

00:20:02.722 --> 00:20:03.723
Now post up.

00:20:03.767 --> 00:20:05.464
We need all the help we can get.

00:20:05.508 --> 00:20:06.509
Prepare to cut power.

00:20:06.552 --> 00:20:07.858
That panel is still up.

00:20:07.901 --> 00:20:09.251
Boimler's got it.
Just give him time.

00:20:09.294 --> 00:20:10.643
We don't have time.

00:20:12.428 --> 00:20:14.081
Come on, come on...

00:20:17.911 --> 00:20:19.652
Got it!

00:20:21.219 --> 00:20:22.307
Panel's free!

00:20:22.351 --> 00:20:24.004
Cut power!

00:20:27.181 --> 00:20:28.661
Ah! Ah! No, no, no!

00:20:28.705 --> 00:20:30.228
No, no, no, no, no!

00:20:50.248 --> 00:20:53.077
Big chunk, starboard,
roughly 55.18 degrees.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.427
And another at 38.20!

00:20:55.471 --> 00:20:57.429
Got it. Hang on to something.

00:21:02.521 --> 00:21:04.480
He should have
come up already.

00:21:04.523 --> 00:21:06.003
Boimler!

00:21:07.396 --> 00:21:08.484
He's in arrest!

00:21:08.527 --> 00:21:09.833
We have to get him to sickbay!

00:21:09.876 --> 00:21:11.051
There's no time!

00:21:18.668 --> 00:21:20.931
Incoming! Direct ahead!

00:21:20.974 --> 00:21:23.325
I can't avoid it!
Brace for impact!

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.680
- Mom!
- Beckett!

00:21:30.723 --> 00:21:32.421
Whoa!

00:21:32.464 --> 00:21:35.293
Okay, come on, Boimler. Come on.

00:21:35.337 --> 00:21:36.686
Come on,
you're going to make it.

00:21:36.729 --> 00:21:38.818
- Boimler! Talk to me.

00:21:38.862 --> 00:21:41.168
Did... did I miss
Captain Freeman Day?

00:21:41.212 --> 00:21:43.475
Yes! He's gonna be okay!

00:21:45.738 --> 00:21:47.218
I saw a koala...

00:21:47.261 --> 00:21:48.828
Uh, yeah, you know,
it's probably best

00:21:48.872 --> 00:21:50.395
you just keep that to yourself.

00:21:57.141 --> 00:21:58.708
No!

00:22:02.799 --> 00:22:04.017
Gotcha.

00:22:14.245 --> 00:22:17.509
Five minutes until
we hit atmosphere, Captain.

00:22:17.553 --> 00:22:19.685
Everyone, if you move
to the back of the ship,

00:22:19.729 --> 00:22:20.991
there's a chance you'll survive.

00:22:21.034 --> 00:22:22.993
Sonya, no.
We are staying with you.

00:22:23.036 --> 00:22:24.647
It has been an honor.

00:22:45.842 --> 00:22:47.496
Wait, what's happening?

00:22:47.539 --> 00:22:48.975
It's the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:57.636 --> 00:23:00.030
The &lt;i&gt;Archimedes&lt;/i&gt; is
in stable orbit, Captain.

00:23:00.073 --> 00:23:01.292
No lives lost.

00:23:01.335 --> 00:23:02.902
Oh...

00:23:14.436 --> 00:23:16.046
Hey, I'm proud of you, Mom.

00:23:16.089 --> 00:23:18.048
You saved the day,
kept it together...

00:23:18.091 --> 00:23:20.180
I guess I understand
why Command was so impressed.

00:23:20.224 --> 00:23:21.399
Thank you.

00:23:21.443 --> 00:23:22.879
But I'm a little nervous.

00:23:24.881 --> 00:23:26.360
How do I look?

00:23:26.404 --> 00:23:28.362
Like a badass captain
who knows what's up.

00:23:29.668 --> 00:23:31.670
On behalf of the United
Federation of Planets,

00:23:31.714 --> 00:23:33.455
allow me to introduce myself.

00:23:33.498 --> 00:23:35.152
I am Captain Carol Freeman,

00:23:35.195 --> 00:23:36.806
of the starship &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:36.849 --> 00:23:38.198
and I come in...

00:23:38.242 --> 00:23:39.504
- Whoa!

00:23:39.548 --> 00:23:40.766
Lapeeria welcomes you!

00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:42.333
We must drink!

00:23:57.391 --> 00:23:59.829
Every time I think
I'm out of this thing,

00:23:59.872 --> 00:24:01.657
boom, hit by an asteroid.

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:03.702
Well, don't worry. I'm sure
you're the doc's top priority.

00:24:03.746 --> 00:24:05.487
Ensign Tendi, get over here.

00:24:07.401 --> 00:24:09.012
Listen, I-I know what
you're going to say,

00:24:09.055 --> 00:24:11.188
and I'm so sorry
for letting you down.

00:24:11.231 --> 00:24:12.972
I-I know
I don't belong in sickbay.

00:24:13.016 --> 00:24:14.017
You're right, you don't.

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:15.671
- You master

00:24:15.714 --> 00:24:17.237
everything you put your mind to.

00:24:17.281 --> 00:24:18.282
It's unsettling.

00:24:18.325 --> 00:24:19.979
Oh, uh, thank you?

00:24:20.023 --> 00:24:21.851
You shouldn't be treating
phaser burns.

00:24:21.894 --> 00:24:24.549
I'm moving you into
senior science officer training.

00:24:24.593 --> 00:24:26.420
Wait, like, to work
on the bridge?

00:24:26.464 --> 00:24:28.205
Like Jadzia Dax?

00:24:28.248 --> 00:24:29.554
Who the is that?
I don't know who that is.

00:24:29.598 --> 00:24:31.077
No, like Spock.

00:24:31.121 --> 00:24:32.905
It means a lot more experiments,
away missions--

00:24:32.949 --> 00:24:34.037
think you can handle it?

00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:36.126
- Thank you so much!

00:24:36.169 --> 00:24:38.171
I'm okay with this.

00:24:42.262 --> 00:24:43.916
Ha! Rutherford!

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.135
I get to stay on the ship!

00:24:45.178 --> 00:24:46.702
And Dr. T'Ana hugged me!

00:24:46.745 --> 00:24:48.834
You do? She did?

00:24:48.878 --> 00:24:50.096
Hey!

00:24:50.140 --> 00:24:52.011
Happy first first contact,
Cap.

00:24:52.055 --> 00:24:53.535
Oh, thank you, Jack.

00:24:53.578 --> 00:24:54.971
It was great.

00:24:55.014 --> 00:24:56.929
Are you--
Have you been drinking?

00:24:56.973 --> 00:24:59.671
They're a very welcoming
culture.

00:24:59.715 --> 00:25:01.760
Repairs on the &lt;i&gt;Archimedes&lt;/i&gt; are
going smoothly.

00:25:01.804 --> 00:25:03.762
Captain Gomez
is recovering nicely.

00:25:03.806 --> 00:25:06.765
It was kind of her
to let me finish the mission.

00:25:06.809 --> 00:25:08.767
No ego on that one.

00:25:08.811 --> 00:25:10.377
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:25:10.421 --> 00:25:12.292
Thanks for doing
a super dangerous space walk

00:25:12.336 --> 00:25:14.991
to save my life.
That was pretty cool.

00:25:15.034 --> 00:25:17.123
No worries. &lt;i&gt;
Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; strong, right?

00:25:17.167 --> 00:25:18.908
Totally.

00:25:18.951 --> 00:25:20.823
Sorry I've been a jerk all year.

00:25:20.866 --> 00:25:22.389
I kind of thought you hated me.

00:25:22.433 --> 00:25:24.870
Yeah, you know,
I think when I like people,

00:25:24.914 --> 00:25:26.350
I maybe go out of my way

00:25:26.393 --> 00:25:28.178
to force some distance,
so that's on me.

00:25:28.221 --> 00:25:30.572
So what I'm taking away
from that was that you like me?

00:25:30.615 --> 00:25:32.574
No. Shut up, come on.

00:25:32.617 --> 00:25:35.620
Congrats, Brad.
You were a real hero today.

00:25:35.664 --> 00:25:38.188
Thanks, but anyone would have
done the same.

00:25:38.231 --> 00:25:39.798
Whoa, check out
Mr. Humble Confidence.

00:25:39.842 --> 00:25:41.365
Where'd you come from?

00:25:41.408 --> 00:25:43.236
I guess when you almost
drown in whale pee,

00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:45.630
it makes you not sweat the
small stuff anymore, you know?

00:25:45.674 --> 00:25:47.458
Oh, Mom noticed the decorations,
by the way.

00:25:47.501 --> 00:25:49.373
What?
D-D-Did she know it was me?

00:25:49.416 --> 00:25:52.028
Mm, she probably assumes
it was children, actually.

00:25:52.071 --> 00:25:54.247
Cap'n! Cap'n!
I drew the banners!

00:25:54.291 --> 00:25:55.597
Huh. I like that guy.

00:25:55.640 --> 00:25:56.946
Right? He's great.

00:25:56.989 --> 00:25:58.121
To the Captain!

00:25:58.164 --> 00:26:00.471
No, no, no. To the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos!&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:00.514 --> 00:26:03.039
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,
I love you!&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:03.082 --> 00:26:05.128
&lt;i&gt;Captain,
a team from Starfleet Command&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:05.171 --> 00:26:06.608
&lt;i&gt;is requesting to come aboard.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:06.651 --> 00:26:09.001
That was fast.
Permission granted.

00:26:09.045 --> 00:26:11.134
Escort them to
the senior conference room.

00:26:11.177 --> 00:26:12.701
If they were impressed
with you before...

00:26:12.744 --> 00:26:15.225
Whew! Today must have
sealed the deal.

00:26:15.268 --> 00:26:17.096
Hey, nobody deserves the
recognition more than you, Mom.

00:26:17.140 --> 00:26:18.663
Nothing would make us prouder

00:26:18.707 --> 00:26:20.404
than seeing you move up
to bigger and better.

00:26:20.447 --> 00:26:22.754
Maybe bigger, but never better.

00:26:22.798 --> 00:26:24.800
I'm turning down the transfer.

00:26:24.843 --> 00:26:26.149
- What?
- But Captain,

00:26:26.192 --> 00:26:27.454
you've been working
so hard for this.

00:26:27.498 --> 00:26:29.413
Yeah, well,
maybe a little too hard.

00:26:29.456 --> 00:26:31.502
It blinded me
to what I already have

00:26:31.545 --> 00:26:33.286
right here on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:33.330 --> 00:26:34.853
What good would a new ship be

00:26:34.897 --> 00:26:36.725
without the best crew
in the fleet?

00:26:36.768 --> 00:26:38.465
Mom! No way!

00:26:38.509 --> 00:26:41.033
Come on, let's go tell them
they wasted their trip.

00:26:41.077 --> 00:26:42.600
Cap'n! Cap'n!
I drew the banners!

00:26:42.644 --> 00:26:44.080
It was Boimler! It was Boimler!

00:26:46.386 --> 00:26:48.693
Captain Freeman.
I'm Commander Mandel.

00:26:48.737 --> 00:26:50.869
Under the authority of
Starfleet Command, you...

00:26:50.913 --> 00:26:53.089
I have to stop you right there,
Commander.

00:26:53.132 --> 00:26:55.004
I'm not leaving the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:55.047 --> 00:26:56.614
I'm afraid
you don't have a choice.

00:26:56.658 --> 00:26:58.747
I'm turning down
the promotion.

00:26:58.790 --> 00:27:00.574
Look, she might not seem
like much to you,

00:27:00.618 --> 00:27:02.794
but this ship is my home.

00:27:02.838 --> 00:27:06.972
You're under arrest for the
destruction of Pakled Planet.

00:27:07.016 --> 00:27:08.931
What? Wh-- What are you
talking about?

00:27:08.974 --> 00:27:10.280
Hey! Let-let her go!

00:27:10.323 --> 00:27:11.368
This is madness!

00:27:11.411 --> 00:27:12.717
Captain! What are your orders?

00:27:12.761 --> 00:27:14.501
Stand down!
What are the charges?

00:27:14.545 --> 00:27:16.982
We have proof that you colluded
with Klingon extremists

00:27:17.026 --> 00:27:20.159
to plant a Varuvian bomb
in the Pakled capital city.

00:27:20.203 --> 00:27:22.074
My God, when did this happen?

00:27:22.118 --> 00:27:24.816
Today, 0900, while you were
conveniently on a mission...

00:27:24.860 --> 00:27:26.731
I'm sure just as planned.

00:27:26.775 --> 00:27:28.559
She had nothing to do with this!

00:27:28.602 --> 00:27:30.822
- That is for a tribunal
to decide.
- I'll kill you!

00:27:30.866 --> 00:27:32.737
Stop. Let them do their job.

00:27:32.781 --> 00:27:33.825
- But Mom...
- Captain...

00:27:33.869 --> 00:27:34.913
That's an order.

00:27:34.957 --> 00:27:36.219
We have the truth on our side.

00:27:36.262 --> 00:27:37.742
And I don't want
the crew finding out

00:27:37.786 --> 00:27:39.439
until we know more.

00:27:39.483 --> 00:27:41.180
Congratulations, Captain!

00:27:41.224 --> 00:27:43.269
- On behalf of the crew...

00:27:43.313 --> 00:27:45.010
Starfleet Security.

00:27:45.054 --> 00:27:46.751
This woman is under arrest.

00:28:11.515 --> 00:28:14.561
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:29:23.369 --> 00:29:27.369
Chirp.
